    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Vinnie Pasquantino** stands as our premier start with a dominant 72.62 efficiency score. The matchup against Rocker is the anchor of our lineup; **Vinnie Pasquantino** benefits from a substantial +14% platoon edge and a favorable SP xERA of 4.30, positioning him to capitalize on the volume in the cleanup spot. **Josh Naylor** and **James Wood** also project as elite anchors. **James Wood** is particularly vital for our goals given our league-wide mandate to prioritize stolen base threats; his leadoff role and solid 0.384 xwOBA against King make him a high-floor play despite the moderate SP xERA. While we are currently waiting on official lineups for **Gabriel Moreno**, **Corbin Carroll**, and **Jose Caballero**, **Corbin Carroll** remains a critical start even against Woo, as his speed profile provides the elite category-specific value we crave, provided he maintains his projected #2 spot.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today involves the outfield depth, specifically the separation between **Tyler Soderstrom** (56.22) and **Seiya Suzuki** (50.44). While **Tyler Soderstrom** holds the edge due to a favorable park factor and a solid #5 order placement, the gap is slim. We opted to lean into **Tyler Soderstrom** to maximize the park environment against Weathers, though **Seiya Suzuki** remained in the discussion until the final optimization run. Conversely, the situation with **Jose Caballero** is a primary concern; despite a park-boosted projection, his placement in the #9 hole and a rough -13% platoon adjustment against Ginn leave him teetering on the edge of our starting floor. With **Mickey Moniak**, **Austin Riley**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, and **Trevor Story** all currently unavailable due to injury or rest, our remaining bench depth\u2014including **Max Muncy**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Zach McKinstry**, **Alex Freeland**, **Kyle Karros**, and **Carson Williams**\u2014will be monitored closely should any late lineup scratches occur. We are keeping a strict eye on the weather and the pending status of **Gabriel Moreno** and **Corbin Carroll** to ensure we aren't burning game caps on players who find themselves out of the batting order.",
